---@class gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation
---@field tabId? string The tab that the location is in. When omitted, the request is applied to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.
---@field segmentId? string The ID of the header, footer or footnote the location is in. An empty segment ID signifies the document's body.

---A ParagraphElement representing an equation.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Equation
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. An Equation may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.

---A document footer.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Footer
---@field content? gcp.docs_v1.StructuralElementList The contents of the footer. The indexes for a footer's content begin at zero.
---@field footerId? string The ID of the footer.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.FooterMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.Footer }

---A document footnote.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Footnote
---@field content? gcp.docs_v1.StructuralElementList The contents of the footnote. The indexes for a footnote's content begin at zero.
---@field footnoteId? string The ID of the footnote.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.FootnoteMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.Footnote }

---A ParagraphElement representing a footnote reference. A footnote reference is the inline content rendered with a number and is used to identify the footnote.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.FootnoteReference
---@field suggestedTextStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTextStyleMap The suggested text style changes to this FootnoteReference, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field footnoteNumber? string The rendered number of this footnote.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this FootnoteReference.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A FootnoteReference may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field footnoteId? string The ID of the footnote that contains the content of this footnote reference.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.GetDocumentsCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---@class gcp.docs_v1.GetDocumentsRequest
---@field documentId string The ID of the document to retrieve.
---@field suggestionsViewMode? gcp.docs_v1.GetDocumentsSuggestionsViewModeEnum|string The suggestions view mode to apply to the document. This allows viewing the document with all suggestions inline, accepted or rejected. If one is not specified, DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS is used.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.docs_v1.GetDocumentsCommentsViewModeEnum|string The comments view mode to apply to the document. This allows viewing the document with comments omitted or included. If one is not specified, COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED is used. If you set comments_view_mode to any value, you must also set include_tabs_content to `true` or use a field mask that references the Document.tabs field (or any subfield). If you set comments_view_mode to COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED, you must also explicitly set suggestions_view_mode to SUGGESTIONS_INLINE. If you set comments_view_mode to COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED or COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS, you may not set suggestions_view_mode to PREVIEW_WITHOUT_SUGGESTIONS or PREVIEW_SUGGESTIONS_ACCEPTED.
---@field includeTabsContent? boolean Whether to populate the `Document.tabs` field instead of the text content fields like `body` and `documentStyle` on `Document`. - When `true`: Document content populates in the `Document.tabs` field instead of the text content fields in `Document`. - When `false`: The content of the document's first tab populates the content fields in `Document` excluding `Document.tabs`. If a document has only one tab, then that tab is used to populate the document content. `Document.tabs` will be empty. If you use a field mask that references the `Document.tabs` field (or any subfield), the API implicitly treats the request as if you set `include_tabs_content` to `true`.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.GetDocumentsSuggestionsViewModeEnum "DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"SUGGESTIONS_INLINE"|"PREVIEW_SUGGESTIONS_ACCEPTED"|"PREVIEW_WITHOUT_SUGGESTIONS"

---A document header.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Header
---@field headerId? string The ID of the header.
---@field content? gcp.docs_v1.StructuralElementList The contents of the header. The indexes for a header's content begin at zero.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.HeaderMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.Header }

---A reference to a heading in this document.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.HeadingLink
---@field id? string The ID of a heading in this document.
---@field tabId? string The ID of the tab containing this heading.

---A ParagraphElement representing a horizontal line.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.HorizontalRule
---@field suggestedTextStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTextStyleMap The suggested text style changes to this HorizontalRule, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this HorizontalRule. Similar to text content, like text runs and footnote references, the text style of a horizontal rule can affect content layout as well as the styling of text inserted next to it.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A HorizontalRule may have multiple insertion IDs if it is a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.

---The properties of an image.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ImageProperties
---@field contrast? number The contrast effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [-1.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect.
---@field contentUri? string A URI to the image with a default lifetime of 30 minutes. This URI is tagged with the account of the requester. Anyone with the URI effectively accesses the image as the original requester. Access to the image may be lost if the document's sharing settings change.
---@field sourceUri? string The source URI is the URI used to insert the image. The source URI can be empty.
---@field transparency? number The transparency effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [0.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect and 1 means transparent.
---@field angle? number The clockwise rotation angle of the image, in radians.
---@field cropProperties? gcp.docs_v1.CropProperties The crop properties of the image.
---@field brightness? number The brightness effect of the image. The value should be in the interval [-1.0, 1.0], where 0 means no effect.

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base ImageProperties have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ImagePropertiesSuggestionState
---@field contrastSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to contrast.
---@field contentUriSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to content_uri.
---@field cropPropertiesSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.CropPropertiesSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in crop_properties have been changed in this suggestion.
---@field transparencySuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to transparency.
---@field brightnessSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to brightness.
---@field angleSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to angle.
---@field sourceUriSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to source_uri.

---An object that appears inline with text. An InlineObject contains an EmbeddedObject such as an image.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InlineObject
---@field suggestedInlineObjectPropertiesChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedInlineObjectPropertiesMap The suggested changes to the inline object properties, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field inlineObjectProperties? gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectProperties The properties of this inline object.
---@field suggestedInsertionId? string The suggested insertion ID. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field objectId? string The ID of this inline object. Can be used to update an object’s properties.

---A ParagraphElement that contains an InlineObject.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectElement
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field inlineObjectId? string The ID of the InlineObject this element contains.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. An InlineObjectElement may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this InlineObjectElement. Similar to text content, like text runs and footnote references, the text style of an inline object element can affect content layout as well as the styling of text inserted next to it.
---@field suggestedTextStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTextStyleMap The suggested text style changes to this InlineObject, keyed by suggestion ID.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.InlineObject }

---Properties of an InlineObject.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectProperties
---@field embeddedObject? gcp.docs_v1.EmbeddedObject The embedded object of this inline object.

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base InlineObjectProperties have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectPropertiesSuggestionState
---@field embeddedObjectSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.EmbeddedObjectSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in embedded_object have been changed in this suggestion.

---Inserts a CommentThread into the document.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertCommentRequest
---@field content? string The text of the comment, as plain text. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Docs editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. This field cannot be empty, and must not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field assigneeEmailAddress? string Optional. The email address of the assignee of the comment. Leave empty for a non-assigned comment. May not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field range? gcp.docs_v1.Range The Range in the document that is tied to this comment.

---Response message for inserting a comment.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertCommentResponse
---@field commentThread? gcp.docs_v1.CommentThread The newly-inserted comment thread.

---Inserts a date at the specified location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertDateRequest
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the date at the end of the given header, footer or document body.
---@field dateElementProperties? gcp.docs_v1.DateElementProperties The properties of the date to insert.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the date at a specific index in the document. The date must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between an existing table and its preceding paragraph).

---Inserts a Dropdown at the specified location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertDropdownRequest
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation The EndOfSegmentLocation in the document to insert the dropdown at.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location The Location in the document to insert the dropdown at.
---@field selectedOptionId? string Optional initial value for the dropdown. If this field is not specified, the new dropdown will default to selecting the first option defined in the dropdown definition. If this field is specified but does not reference a valid option in the dropdown definition, a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field dropdownDefinitionId? string Required. The DropdownDefinition ID.

---The result of inserting a Dropdown.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertDropdownResponse
---@field dropdown? gcp.docs_v1.Dropdown The newly-inserted Dropdown.

---Inserts an InlineObject containing an image at the given location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertInlineImageRequest
---@field objectSize? gcp.docs_v1.Size The size that the image should appear as in the document. This property is optional and the final size of the image in the document is determined by the following rules: * If neither width nor height is specified, then a default size of the image is calculated based on its resolution. * If one dimension is specified then the other dimension is calculated to preserve the aspect ratio of the image. * If both width and height are specified, the image is scaled to fit within the provided dimensions while maintaining its aspect ratio.
---@field uri? string The image URI. The image is fetched once at insertion time and a copy is stored for display inside the document. Images must be less than 50MB in size, cannot exceed 25 megapixels, and must be in one of PNG, JPEG, or GIF format. The provided URI must be publicly accessible and at most 2 kB in length. The URI itself is saved with the image, and exposed via the ImageProperties.content_uri field.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the image at a specific index in the document. The image must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). Inline images cannot be inserted inside a footnote or equation.
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the text at the end of a header, footer or the document body. Inline images cannot be inserted inside a footnote.

---The result of inserting an inline image.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertInlineImageResponse
---@field objectId? string The ID of the created InlineObject.

---The result of inserting an embedded Google Sheets chart.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertInlineSheetsChartResponse
---@field objectId? string The object ID of the inserted chart.

---Inserts a page break followed by a newline at the specified location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertPageBreakRequest
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the page break at a specific index in the document. The page break must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). Page breaks cannot be inserted inside a table, equation, footnote, header or footer. Since page breaks can only be inserted inside the body, the segment ID field must be empty.
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the page break at the end of the document body. Page breaks cannot be inserted inside a footnote, header or footer. Since page breaks can only be inserted inside the body, the segment ID field must be empty.

---Inserts a person mention.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertPersonRequest
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the person mention at the end of a header, footer, footnote or the document body.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the person mention at a specific index in the document. The person mention must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). Person mentions cannot be inserted inside an equation.
---@field personProperties? gcp.docs_v1.PersonProperties The properties of the person mention to insert.

---Inserts a RichLink at the specified location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertRichLinkRequest
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the rich link at the end of a header, footer, footnote or the document body.
---@field richLinkProperties? gcp.docs_v1.RichLinkProperties The properties of the rich link to insert.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the rich link at a specific index in the document. The rich link must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). The rich link cannot be inserted inside an equation.

---Inserts a section break at the given location. A newline character will be inserted before the section break.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertSectionBreakRequest
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts a newline and a section break at a specific index in the document. The section break must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). Section breaks cannot be inserted inside a table, equation, footnote, header, or footer. Since section breaks can only be inserted inside the body, the segment ID field must be empty.
---@field sectionType? gcp.docs_v1.InsertSectionBreakRequestSectionTypeEnum|string The type of section to insert.
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts a newline and a section break at the end of the document body. Section breaks cannot be inserted inside a footnote, header or footer. Because section breaks can only be inserted inside the body, the segment ID field must be empty.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.InsertSectionBreakRequestSectionTypeEnum "SECTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTINUOUS"|"NEXT_PAGE"

---Inserts an empty column into a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertTableColumnRequest
---@field insertRight? boolean Whether to insert new column to the right of the reference cell location. - `True`: insert to the right. - `False`: insert to the left.
---@field tableCellLocation? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which columns will be inserted. A new column will be inserted to the left (or right) of the column where the reference cell is. If the reference cell is a merged cell, a new column will be inserted to the left (or right) of the merged cell.

---Inserts a table at the specified location. A newline character will be inserted before the inserted table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertTableRequest
---@field rows? number The number of rows in the table.
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the table at the end of the given header, footer or document body. A newline character will be inserted before the inserted table. Tables cannot be inserted inside a footnote.
---@field columns? number The number of columns in the table.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the table at a specific model index. A newline character will be inserted before the inserted table, therefore the table start index will be at the specified location index + 1. The table must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, it cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between an existing table and its preceding paragraph). Tables cannot be inserted inside a footnote or equation.

---Inserts an empty row into a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertTableRowRequest
---@field insertBelow? boolean Whether to insert new row below the reference cell location. - `True`: insert below the cell. - `False`: insert above the cell.
---@field tableCellLocation? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellLocation The reference table cell location from which rows will be inserted. A new row will be inserted above (or below) the row where the reference cell is. If the reference cell is a merged cell, a new row will be inserted above (or below) the merged cell.

---Inserts text at the specified location.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.InsertTextRequest
---@field endOfSegmentLocation? gcp.docs_v1.EndOfSegmentLocation Inserts the text at the end of a header, footer, footnote or the document body.
---@field location? gcp.docs_v1.Location Inserts the text at a specific index in the document. Text must be inserted inside the bounds of an existing Paragraph. For instance, text cannot be inserted at a table's start index (i.e. between the table and its preceding paragraph). The text must be inserted in the preceding paragraph.
---@field text? string The text to be inserted. Inserting a newline character will implicitly create a new Paragraph at that index. The paragraph style of the new paragraph will be copied from the paragraph at the current insertion index, including lists and bullets. Text styles for inserted text will be determined automatically, generally preserving the styling of neighboring text. In most cases, the text style for the inserted text will match the text immediately before the insertion index. Some control characters (U+0000-U+0008, U+000C-U+001F) and characters from the Unicode Basic Multilingual Plane Private Use Area (U+E000-U+F8FF) will be stripped out of the inserted text.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.IntegerList number[]

---A reference to another portion of a document or an external URL resource.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Link
---@field bookmarkId? string The ID of a bookmark in this document. Legacy field: Instead, set includeTabsContent to `true` and use Link.bookmark for read and write operations. This field is only returned when includeTabsContent is set to `false` in documents containing a single tab and links to a bookmark within the singular tab. Otherwise, Link.bookmark is returned. If this field is used in a write request, the bookmark is considered to be from the tab ID specified in the request. If a tab ID is not specified in the request, it is considered to be from the first tab in the document.
---@field url? string An external URL.
---@field bookmark? gcp.docs_v1.BookmarkLink A bookmark in this document. In documents containing a single tab, links to bookmarks within the singular tab continue to return Link.bookmarkId when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `false` or unset. Otherwise, this field is returned.
---@field headingId? string The ID of a heading in this document. Legacy field: Instead, set includeTabsContent to `true` and use Link.heading for read and write operations. This field is only returned when includeTabsContent is set to `false` in documents containing a single tab and links to a heading within the singular tab. Otherwise, Link.heading is returned. If this field is used in a write request, the heading is considered to be from the tab ID specified in the request. If a tab ID is not specified in the request, it is considered to be from the first tab in the document.
---@field tabId? string The ID of a tab in this document.
---@field heading? gcp.docs_v1.HeadingLink A heading in this document. In documents containing a single tab, links to headings within the singular tab continue to return Link.headingId when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `false` or unset. Otherwise, this field is returned.

---A reference to the external linked source content.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.LinkedContentReference
---@field sheetsChartReference? gcp.docs_v1.SheetsChartReference A reference to the linked chart.

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base LinkedContentReference have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.LinkedContentReferenceSuggestionState
---@field sheetsChartReferenceSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.SheetsChartReferenceSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in sheets_chart_reference have been changed in this suggestion.

---A List represents the list attributes for a group of paragraphs that all belong to the same list. A paragraph that's part of a list has a reference to the list's ID in its bullet.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.List
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this list.
---@field listProperties? gcp.docs_v1.ListProperties The properties of the list.
---@field suggestedInsertionId? string The suggested insertion ID. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field suggestedListPropertiesChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedListPropertiesMap The suggested changes to the list properties, keyed by suggestion ID.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ListMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.List }

---The properties of a list that describe the look and feel of bullets belonging to paragraphs associated with a list.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ListProperties
---@field nestingLevels? gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelList Describes the properties of the bullets at the associated level. A list has at most 9 levels of nesting with nesting level 0 corresponding to the top-most level and nesting level 8 corresponding to the most nested level. The nesting levels are returned in ascending order with the least nested returned first.

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base ListProperties have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ListPropertiesSuggestionState
---@field nestingLevelsSuggestionStates? gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelSuggestionStateList A mask that indicates which of the fields on the corresponding NestingLevel in nesting_levels have been changed in this suggestion. The nesting level suggestion states are returned in ascending order of the nesting level with the least nested returned first.

---A particular location in the document.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Location
---@field segmentId? string The ID of the header, footer or footnote the location is in. An empty segment ID signifies the document's body.
---@field index? number The zero-based index, in UTF-16 code units. The index is relative to the beginning of the segment specified by segment_id.
---@field tabId? string The tab that the location is in. When omitted, the request is applied to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.

---Merges cells in a Table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.MergeTableCellsRequest
---@field tableRange? gcp.docs_v1.TableRange The table range specifying which cells of the table to merge. Any text in the cells being merged will be concatenated and stored in the "head" cell of the range. This is the upper-left cell of the range when the content direction is left to right, and the upper-right cell of the range otherwise. If the range is non-rectangular (which can occur in some cases where the range covers cells that are already merged or where the table is non-rectangular), a 400 bad request error is returned.

---A collection of Ranges with the same named range ID. Named ranges allow developers to associate parts of a document with an arbitrary user-defined label so their contents can be programmatically read or edited later. A document can contain multiple named ranges with the same name, but every named range has a unique ID. A named range is created with a single Range, and content inserted inside a named range generally expands that range. However, certain document changes can cause the range to be split into multiple ranges. Named ranges are not private. All applications and collaborators that have access to the document can see its named ranges.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedRange
---@field namedRangeId? string The ID of the named range.
---@field name? string The name of the named range.
---@field ranges? gcp.docs_v1.RangeList The ranges that belong to this named range.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedRangeList gcp.docs_v1.NamedRange[]

---A collection of all the NamedRanges in the document that share a given name.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedRanges
---@field name? string The name that all the named ranges share.
---@field namedRanges? gcp.docs_v1.NamedRangeList The NamedRanges that share the same name.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedRangesMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.NamedRanges }

---A named style. Paragraphs in the document can inherit their TextStyle and ParagraphStyle from this named style when they have the same named style type.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyle
---@field namedStyleType? gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleNamedStyleTypeEnum|string The type of this named style.
---@field paragraphStyle? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyle The paragraph style of this named style.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this named style.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleList gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyle[]

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleNamedStyleTypeEnum "NAMED_STYLE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL_TEXT"|"TITLE"|"SUBTITLE"|"HEADING_1"|"HEADING_2"|"HEADING_3"|"HEADING_4"|"HEADING_5"|"HEADING_6"

---A suggestion state of a NamedStyle message.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionState
---@field paragraphStyleSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in paragraph style have been changed in this suggestion.
---@field textStyleSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyleSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in text style have been changed in this suggestion.
---@field namedStyleType? gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionStateNamedStyleTypeEnum|string The named style type that this suggestion state corresponds to. This field is provided as a convenience for matching the NamedStyleSuggestionState with its corresponding NamedStyle.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionStateList gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionState[]

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionStateNamedStyleTypeEnum "NAMED_STYLE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL_TEXT"|"TITLE"|"SUBTITLE"|"HEADING_1"|"HEADING_2"|"HEADING_3"|"HEADING_4"|"HEADING_5"|"HEADING_6"

---The named styles. Paragraphs in the document can inherit their TextStyle and ParagraphStyle from these named styles.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyles
---@field styles? gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleList The named styles. There's an entry for each of the possible named style types.

---The suggestion state of a NamedStyles message.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NamedStylesSuggestionState
---@field stylesSuggestionStates? gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyleSuggestionStateList A mask that indicates which of the fields on the corresponding NamedStyle in styles have been changed in this suggestion. The order of these named style suggestion states matches the order of the corresponding named style within the named styles suggestion.

---Contains properties describing the look and feel of a list bullet at a given level of nesting.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevel
---@field bulletAlignment? gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelBulletAlignmentEnum|string The alignment of the bullet within the space allotted for rendering the bullet.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of bullets at this level of nesting.
---@field glyphSymbol? string A custom glyph symbol used by bullets when paragraphs at this level of nesting is unordered. The glyph symbol replaces placeholders within the glyph_format. For example, if the glyph_symbol is the solid circle corresponding to Unicode U+25cf code point and the glyph_format is `%0`, the rendered glyph would be the solid circle.
---@field indentStart? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for paragraphs at this level of nesting. Applied to the side that corresponds to the start of the text, based on the paragraph's content direction.
---@field glyphFormat? string The format string used by bullets at this level of nesting. The glyph format contains one or more placeholders, and these placeholders are replaced with the appropriate values depending on the glyph_type or glyph_symbol. The placeholders follow the pattern `%[nesting_level]`. Furthermore, placeholders can have prefixes and suffixes. Thus, the glyph format follows the pattern `%[nesting_level]`. Note that the prefix and suffix are optional and can be arbitrary strings. For example, the glyph format `%0.` indicates that the rendered glyph will replace the placeholder with the corresponding glyph for nesting level 0 followed by a period as the suffix. So a list with a glyph type of UPPER_ALPHA and glyph format `%0.` at nesting level 0 will result in a list with rendered glyphs `A.` `B.` `C.` The glyph format can contain placeholders for the current nesting level as well as placeholders for parent nesting levels. For example, a list can have a glyph format of `%0.` at nesting level 0 and a glyph format of `%0.%1.` at nesting level 1. Assuming both nesting levels have DECIMAL glyph types, this would result in a list with rendered glyphs `1.` `2.` ` 2.1.` ` 2.2.` `3.` For nesting levels that are ordered, the string that replaces a placeholder in the glyph format for a particular paragraph depends on the paragraph's order within the list.
---@field startNumber? number The number of the first list item at this nesting level. A value of 0 is treated as a value of 1 for lettered lists and Roman numeral lists. For values of both 0 and 1, lettered and Roman numeral lists will begin at `a` and `i` respectively. This value is ignored for nesting levels with unordered glyphs.
---@field glyphType? gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelGlyphTypeEnum|string The type of glyph used by bullets when paragraphs at this level of nesting is ordered. The glyph type determines the type of glyph used to replace placeholders within the glyph_format when paragraphs at this level of nesting are ordered. For example, if the nesting level is 0, the glyph_format is `%0.` and the glyph type is DECIMAL, then the rendered glyph would replace the placeholder `%0` in the glyph format with a number corresponding to the list item's order within the list.
---@field indentFirstLine? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for the first line of paragraphs at this level of nesting.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelBulletAlignmentEnum "BULLET_ALIGNMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"START"|"CENTER"|"END"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelGlyphTypeEnum "GLYPH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"DECIMAL"|"ZERO_DECIMAL"|"UPPER_ALPHA"|"ALPHA"|"UPPER_ROMAN"|"ROMAN"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelList gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevel[]

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base NestingLevel have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelSuggestionState
---@field glyphSymbolSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to glyph_symbol.
---@field indentStartSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to indent_start.
---@field startNumberSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to start_number.
---@field glyphTypeSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to glyph_type.
---@field textStyleSuggestionState? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyleSuggestionState A mask that indicates which of the fields in text style have been changed in this suggestion.
---@field indentFirstLineSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to indent_first_line.
---@field bulletAlignmentSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to bullet_alignment.
---@field glyphFormatSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to glyph_format.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelSuggestionStateList gcp.docs_v1.NestingLevelSuggestionState[]

---A collection of object IDs.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ObjectReferences
---@field objectIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The object IDs.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ObjectReferencesMap { [string]: gcp.docs_v1.ObjectReferences }

---A color that can either be fully opaque or fully transparent.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.OptionalColor
---@field color? gcp.docs_v1.Color If set, this will be used as an opaque color. If unset, this represents a transparent color.

---A ParagraphElement representing a page break. A page break makes the subsequent text start at the top of the next page.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.PageBreak
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A PageBreak may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field suggestedTextStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTextStyleMap The suggested text style changes to this PageBreak, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this PageBreak. Similar to text content, like text runs and footnote references, the text style of a page break can affect content layout as well as the styling of text inserted next to it.

---A StructuralElement representing a paragraph. A paragraph is a range of content that's terminated with a newline character.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Paragraph
---@field elements? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphElementList The content of the paragraph, broken down into its component parts.
---@field bullet? gcp.docs_v1.Bullet The bullet for this paragraph. If not present, the paragraph does not belong to a list.
---@field suggestedBulletChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedBulletMap The suggested changes to this paragraph's bullet.
---@field paragraphStyle? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyle The style of this paragraph.
---@field positionedObjectIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The IDs of the positioned objects tethered to this paragraph.
---@field suggestedParagraphStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedParagraphStyleMap The suggested paragraph style changes to this paragraph, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field suggestedPositionedObjectIds? gcp.docs_v1.ObjectReferencesMap The IDs of the positioned objects suggested to be attached to this paragraph, keyed by suggestion ID.

