---@field startIndex? number The zero-based start index of this paragraph element, in UTF-16 code units.
---@field inlineObjectElement? gcp.docs_v1.InlineObjectElement An inline object paragraph element.
---@field dropdown? gcp.docs_v1.Dropdown A paragraph element that represents a dropdown menu.
---@field equation? gcp.docs_v1.Equation An equation paragraph element.
---@field dateElement? gcp.docs_v1.DateElement A paragraph element that represents a date.
---@field endIndex? number The zero-base end index of this paragraph element, exclusive, in UTF-16 code units.
---@field horizontalRule? gcp.docs_v1.HorizontalRule A horizontal rule paragraph element.
---@field footnoteReference? gcp.docs_v1.FootnoteReference A footnote reference paragraph element.
---@field autoText? gcp.docs_v1.AutoText An auto text paragraph element.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphElementList gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphElement[]

---Styles that apply to a whole paragraph. Inherited paragraph styles are represented as unset fields in this message. A paragraph style's parent depends on where the paragraph style is defined: * The ParagraphStyle on a Paragraph inherits from the paragraph's corresponding named style type. * The ParagraphStyle on a named style inherits from the normal text named style. * The ParagraphStyle of the normal text named style inherits from the default paragraph style in the Docs editor. * The ParagraphStyle on a Paragraph element that's contained in a table may inherit its paragraph style from the table style. If the paragraph style does not inherit from a parent, unsetting fields will revert the style to a value matching the defaults in the Docs editor.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyle
---@field direction? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleDirectionEnum|string The text direction of this paragraph. If unset, the value defaults to LEFT_TO_RIGHT since paragraph direction is not inherited.
---@field keepWithNext? boolean Whether at least a part of this paragraph should be laid out on the same page or column as the next paragraph if possible. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field indentFirstLine? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for the first line of the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field pageBreakBefore? boolean Whether the current paragraph should always start at the beginning of a page. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. Attempting to update page_break_before for paragraphs in unsupported regions, including Table, Header, Footer and Footnote, can result in an invalid document state that returns a 400 bad request error.
---@field tabStops? gcp.docs_v1.TabStopList A list of the tab stops for this paragraph. The list of tab stops is not inherited. This property is read-only.
---@field borderBottom? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphBorder The border at the bottom of this paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. The bottom border is rendered when the paragraph below has different border and indent properties. Paragraph borders cannot be partially updated. When changing a paragraph border, the new border must be specified in its entirety.
---@field keepLinesTogether? boolean Whether all lines of the paragraph should be laid out on the same page or column if possible. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field indentEnd? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for the paragraph on the side that corresponds to the end of the text, based on the current paragraph direction. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field borderRight? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphBorder The border to the right of this paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. Paragraph borders cannot be partially updated. When changing a paragraph border, the new border must be specified in its entirety.
---@field indentStart? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of indentation for the paragraph on the side that corresponds to the start of the text, based on the current paragraph direction. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field spaceBelow? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of extra space below the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field avoidWidowAndOrphan? boolean Whether to avoid widows and orphans for the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field borderBetween? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphBorder The border between this paragraph and the next and previous paragraphs. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. The between border is rendered when the adjacent paragraph has the same border and indent properties. Paragraph borders cannot be partially updated. When changing a paragraph border, the new border must be specified in its entirety.
---@field alignment? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleAlignmentEnum|string The text alignment for this paragraph.
---@field borderLeft? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphBorder The border to the left of this paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. Paragraph borders cannot be partially updated. When changing a paragraph border, the new border must be specified in its entirety.
---@field lineSpacing? number The amount of space between lines, as a percentage of normal, where normal is represented as 100.0. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field spacingMode? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleSpacingModeEnum|string The spacing mode for the paragraph.
---@field headingId? string The heading ID of the paragraph. If empty, then this paragraph is not a heading. This property is read-only.
---@field borderTop? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphBorder The border at the top of this paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent. The top border is rendered when the paragraph above has different border and indent properties. Paragraph borders cannot be partially updated. When changing a paragraph border, the new border must be specified in its entirety.
---@field spaceAbove? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The amount of extra space above the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.
---@field namedStyleType? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleNamedStyleTypeEnum|string The named style type of the paragraph. Since updating the named style type affects other properties within ParagraphStyle, the named style type is applied before the other properties are updated.
---@field shading? gcp.docs_v1.Shading The shading of the paragraph. If unset, the value is inherited from the parent.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleAlignmentEnum "ALIGNMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"START"|"CENTER"|"END"|"JUSTIFIED"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleDirectionEnum "CONTENT_DIRECTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"|"RIGHT_TO_LEFT"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleNamedStyleTypeEnum "NAMED_STYLE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL_TEXT"|"TITLE"|"SUBTITLE"|"HEADING_1"|"HEADING_2"|"HEADING_3"|"HEADING_4"|"HEADING_5"|"HEADING_6"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyleSpacingModeEnum "SPACING_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NEVER_COLLAPSE"|"COLLAPSE_LISTS"

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base ParagraphStyle have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
