---Represents a single post in a comment or suggestion thread.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Post
---@field postId? string Output only. The unique ID of the post.
---@field fromDocumentComparison? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from a document comparison. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field deleted? boolean Output only. Whether the post is deleted. If `true`, content and author fields will be empty.
---@field assigneeEmail? string Optional. The email of the user who is being newly assigned to the thread as part of this post. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The parent thread is a CommentThread whose headPost does not have an assignee. - The parent thread is a SuggestionThread. - commentAction is specified as `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. - `assigneeEmail` exceeds 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field author? gcp.docs_v1.PostAuthor Output only. The user who created the post.
---@field content? string The content of the post. Required to be non-empty if commentAction is not `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Docs editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. May not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field commentAction? gcp.docs_v1.PostCommentActionEnum|string Optional. The action type for comment posts.
---@field fromCopiedDocument? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from a copied document. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field fromImportedDocument? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from an imported document. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the post was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the post was last updated.
---@field contentHtml? string Output only. The content of the post as HTML.
---@field suggestionAction? gcp.docs_v1.PostSuggestionActionEnum|string Output only. The action type for suggestion posts.

---Represents a user who authored a comment or suggestion post.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.PostAuthor
---@field displayName? string The display name of the user. May be absent if the author is anonymous.
---@field me? boolean Whether the user is the authenticated user making the request.
---@field user? string The resource name of the post author user, which can also be used to identify the user in the [Google People API](https://developers.google.com/people/api/rest/v1/people). Format: `users/{user}`. Will not be populated if the anonymous field is `true` or if the post is from an imported document.
---@field anonymous? boolean Whether the user is anonymous.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.PostCommentActionEnum "COMMENT_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_COMMENT_ACTION_CHANGE"|"RESOLVE"|"REOPEN"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.PostList gcp.docs_v1.Post[]

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.PostSuggestionActionEnum "SUGGESTION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_SUGGESTION_ACTION_CHANGE"|"ACCEPT"|"REJECT"

---Specifies a contiguous range of text.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Range
---@field endIndex? number The zero-based end index of this range, exclusive, in UTF-16 code units. In all current uses, an end index must be provided. This field is an Int32Value in order to accommodate future use cases with open-ended ranges.
---@field startIndex? number The zero-based start index of this range, in UTF-16 code units. In all current uses, a start index must be provided. This field is an Int32Value in order to accommodate future use cases with open-ended ranges.
---@field tabId? string The tab that contains this range. When omitted, the request applies to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.
---@field segmentId? string The ID of the header, footer, or footnote that this range is contained in. An empty segment ID signifies the document's body.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.RangeList gcp.docs_v1.Range[]

---Rejects a suggestion. Returns a 403 forbidden error if the requesting user does not have edit access to the document and is not the author of the suggestion.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.RejectSuggestionRequest
---@field suggestionId? string The ID of the suggestion.

---Replaces all instances of text matching a criteria with replace text.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceAllTextRequest
---@field tabsCriteria? gcp.docs_v1.TabsCriteria Optional. The criteria used to specify in which tabs the replacement occurs. When omitted, the replacement applies to all tabs. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the replacement applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the replacement applies to the specified tabs. - If omitted, the replacement applies to all tabs.
---@field replaceText? string The text that will replace the matched text.
---@field containsText? gcp.docs_v1.SubstringMatchCriteria Finds text in the document matching this substring.

---The result of replacing text.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceAllTextResponse
---@field occurrencesChanged? number The number of occurrences changed by replacing all text.

---Replaces an existing image with a new image. Replacing an image removes some image effects from the existing image in order to mirror the behavior of the Docs editor.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceImageRequest
---@field tabId? string The tab that the image to be replaced is in. When omitted, the request is applied to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.
---@field imageObjectId? string The ID of the existing image that will be replaced. The ID can be retrieved from the response of a get request.
---@field uri? string The URI of the new image. The image is fetched once at insertion time and a copy is stored for display inside the document. Images must be less than 50MB, cannot exceed 25 megapixels, and must be in PNG, JPEG, or GIF format. The provided URI can't surpass 2 KB in length. The URI is saved with the image, and exposed through the ImageProperties.source_uri field.
---@field imageReplaceMethod? gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum|string The replacement method.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceImageRequestImageReplaceMethodEnum "IMAGE_REPLACE_METHOD_UNSPECIFIED"|"CENTER_CROP"

---Replaces the contents of the specified NamedRange or NamedRanges with the given replacement content. Note that an individual NamedRange may consist of multiple discontinuous ranges. In this case, only the content in the first range will be replaced. The other ranges and their content will be deleted. In cases where replacing or deleting any ranges would result in an invalid document structure, a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.ReplaceNamedRangeContentRequest
---@field tabsCriteria? gcp.docs_v1.TabsCriteria Optional. The criteria used to specify in which tabs the replacement occurs. When omitted, the replacement applies to all tabs. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the replacement applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the replacement applies to the specified tabs. - If omitted, the replacement applies to all tabs.
---@field text? string Replaces the content of the specified named range(s) with the given text.
---@field namedRangeId? string The ID of the named range whose content will be replaced. If there is no named range with the given ID a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field namedRangeName? string The name of the NamedRanges whose content will be replaced. If there are multiple named ranges with the given name, then the content of each one will be replaced. If there are no named ranges with the given name, then the request will be a no-op.

---A single update to apply to a document.
