---@field updatedSummarySuggestionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The IDs of suggestions whose summaries were updated during the update.
---@field createdSuggestionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The IDs of suggestions which were created during the update.
---@field deletedSuggestionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The IDs of suggestions which were deleted during the update.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionResponseList gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionResponse[]

---Represents a single suggestion thread. Suggestion threads are created as a byproduct of saving changes to the document while in suggestion mode, and cannot be created directly.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionThread
---@field status? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionThreadStatusEnum|string Whether the thread is open, accepted, or rejected.
---@field headPost? gcp.docs_v1.Post The first post in the thread.
---@field summaryText? string Summary of the suggested differences in the document, in plain text. May be empty.
---@field replies? gcp.docs_v1.PostList Replies to the head post.
---@field suggestionId? string The unique ID of the suggestion.
---@field summaryHtml? string Summary of the suggested differences in the document, in HTML. May be empty.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionThreadList gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionThread[]

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.SuggestionThreadStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"OPEN"|"ACCEPTED"|"REJECTED"

---A tab in a document.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Tab
---@field childTabs? gcp.docs_v1.TabList The child tabs nested within this tab.
---@field documentTab? gcp.docs_v1.DocumentTab A tab with document contents, like text and images.
---@field tabProperties? gcp.docs_v1.TabProperties The properties of the tab, like ID and title.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TabList gcp.docs_v1.Tab[]

---Properties of a tab.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TabProperties
---@field iconEmoji? string Optional. The emoji icon displayed with the tab. A valid emoji icon is represented by a non-empty Unicode string. Any set of characters that don't represent a single emoji is invalid. If an emoji is invalid, a 400 bad request error is returned. If this value is unset or empty, the tab will display the default tab icon.
---@field tabId? string The immutable ID of the tab.
---@field index? number The zero-based index of the tab within the parent.
---@field parentTabId? string Optional. The ID of the parent tab. Empty when the current tab is a root-level tab, which means it doesn't have any parents.
---@field nestingLevel? number Output only. The depth of the tab within the document. Root-level tabs start at 0.
---@field title? string The user-visible name of the tab.

---A tab stop within a paragraph.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TabStop
---@field alignment? gcp.docs_v1.TabStopAlignmentEnum|string The alignment of this tab stop. If unset, the value defaults to START.
---@field offset? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The offset between this tab stop and the start margin.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TabStopAlignmentEnum "TAB_STOP_ALIGNMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"START"|"CENTER"|"END"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TabStopList gcp.docs_v1.TabStop[]

---A StructuralElement representing a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.Table
---@field rows? number Number of rows in the table.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A Table may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field tableStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableStyle The style of the table.
---@field tableRows? gcp.docs_v1.TableRowList The contents and style of each row.
---@field columns? number Number of columns in the table. It's possible for a table to be non-rectangular, so some rows may have a different number of cells.

---The contents and style of a cell in a Table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableCell
---@field content? gcp.docs_v1.StructuralElementList The content of the cell.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A TableCell may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field tableCellStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyle The style of the cell.
---@field startIndex? number The zero-based start index of this cell, in UTF-16 code units.
---@field suggestedTableCellStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTableCellStyleMap The suggested changes to the table cell style, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field endIndex? number The zero-based end index of this cell, exclusive, in UTF-16 code units.

---A border around a table cell. Table cell borders cannot be transparent. To hide a table cell border, make its width 0.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorder
---@field dashStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorderDashStyleEnum|string The dash style of the border.
---@field color? gcp.docs_v1.OptionalColor The color of the border. This color cannot be transparent.
---@field width? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The width of the border.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorderDashStyleEnum "DASH_STYLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLID"|"DOT"|"DASH"

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableCellList gcp.docs_v1.TableCell[]

---Location of a single cell within a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableCellLocation
---@field columnIndex? number The zero-based column index. For example, the second column in the table has a column index of 1.
---@field rowIndex? number The zero-based row index. For example, the second row in the table has a row index of 1.
---@field tableStartLocation? gcp.docs_v1.Location The location where the table starts in the document.

---The style of a TableCell. Inherited table cell styles are represented as unset fields in this message. A table cell style can inherit from the table's style.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyle
---@field borderTop? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorder The top border of the cell.
---@field paddingLeft? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The left padding of the cell.
---@field contentAlignment? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyleContentAlignmentEnum|string The alignment of the content in the table cell. The default alignment matches the alignment for newly created table cells in the Docs editor.
---@field columnSpan? number The column span of the cell. This property is read-only.
---@field borderLeft? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorder The left border of the cell.
---@field paddingBottom? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The bottom padding of the cell.
---@field backgroundColor? gcp.docs_v1.OptionalColor The background color of the cell.
---@field paddingRight? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The right padding of the cell.
---@field borderRight? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorder The right border of the cell.
---@field borderBottom? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellBorder The bottom border of the cell.
---@field paddingTop? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The top padding of the cell.
---@field rowSpan? number The row span of the cell. This property is read-only.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyleContentAlignmentEnum "CONTENT_ALIGNMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONTENT_ALIGNMENT_UNSUPPORTED"|"TOP"|"MIDDLE"|"BOTTOM"

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base TableCellStyle have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyleSuggestionState
---@field paddingTopSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to padding_top.
---@field paddingBottomSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to padding_bottom.
---@field borderTopSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to border_top.
---@field paddingRightSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to padding_right.
---@field backgroundColorSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to background_color.
---@field borderRightSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to border_right.
---@field rowSpanSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to row_span.
---@field borderLeftSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to border_left.
---@field borderBottomSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to border_bottom.
---@field columnSpanSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to column_span.
---@field contentAlignmentSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to content_alignment.
---@field paddingLeftSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to padding_left.

---The properties of a column in a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnProperties
---@field widthType? gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnPropertiesWidthTypeEnum|string The width type of the column.
---@field width? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The width of the column. Set when the column's `width_type` is FIXED_WIDTH.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnPropertiesList gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnProperties[]

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnPropertiesWidthTypeEnum "WIDTH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EVENLY_DISTRIBUTED"|"FIXED_WIDTH"

---A StructuralElement representing a table of contents.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableOfContents
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A TableOfContents may have multiple insertion IDs if it is a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field content? gcp.docs_v1.StructuralElementList The content of the table of contents.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.

---A table range represents a reference to a subset of a table. It's important to note that the cells specified by a table range do not necessarily form a rectangle. For example, let's say we have a 3 x 3 table where all the cells of the last row are merged together. The table looks like this: [ ] A table range with table cell location = (table_start_location, row = 0, column = 0), row span = 3 and column span = 2 specifies the following cells: x x [ x x x ]
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableRange
---@field columnSpan? number The column span of the table range.
---@field tableCellLocation? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellLocation The cell location where the table range starts.
---@field rowSpan? number The row span of the table range.

---The contents and style of a row in a Table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableRow
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A TableRow may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field endIndex? number The zero-based end index of this row, exclusive, in UTF-16 code units.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.
---@field startIndex? number The zero-based start index of this row, in UTF-16 code units.
---@field tableRowStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableRowStyle The style of the table row.
---@field suggestedTableRowStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTableRowStyleMap The suggested style changes to this row, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field tableCells? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellList The contents and style of each cell in this row. It's possible for a table to be non-rectangular, so some rows may have a different number of cells than other rows in the same table.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TableRowList gcp.docs_v1.TableRow[]

---Styles that apply to a table row.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableRowStyle
---@field minRowHeight? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The minimum height of the row. The row will be rendered in the Docs editor at a height equal to or greater than this value in order to show all the content in the row's cells.
---@field tableHeader? boolean Whether the row is a table header.
---@field preventOverflow? boolean Whether the row cannot overflow across page or column boundaries.

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base TableRowStyle have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableRowStyleSuggestionState
---@field minRowHeightSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to min_row_height.

---Styles that apply to a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TableStyle
---@field tableColumnProperties? gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnPropertiesList The properties of each column. Note that in Docs, tables contain rows and rows contain cells, similar to HTML. So the properties for a row can be found on the row's table_row_style.

---A criteria that specifies in which tabs a request executes.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TabsCriteria
---@field tabIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The list of tab IDs in which the request executes.

---A ParagraphElement that represents a run of text that all has the same styling.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TextRun
---@field suggestedTextStyleChanges? gcp.docs_v1.SuggestedTextStyleMap The suggested text style changes to this run, keyed by suggestion ID.
---@field content? string The text of this run. Any non-text elements in the run are replaced with the Unicode character U+E907.
---@field suggestedInsertionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested insertion IDs. A TextRun may have multiple insertion IDs if it's a nested suggested change. If empty, then this is not a suggested insertion.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The text style of this run.
---@field suggestedDeletionIds? gcp.docs_v1.StringList The suggested deletion IDs. If empty, then there are no suggested deletions of this content.

---Represents the styling that can be applied to text. Inherited text styles are represented as unset fields in this message. A text style's parent depends on where the text style is defined: * The TextStyle of text in a Paragraph inherits from the paragraph's corresponding named style type. * The TextStyle on a named style inherits from the normal text named style. * The TextStyle of the normal text named style inherits from the default text style in the Docs editor. * The TextStyle on a Paragraph element that's contained in a table may inherit its text style from the table style. If the text style does not inherit from a parent, unsetting fields will revert the style to a value matching the defaults in the Docs editor.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle
---@field backgroundColor? gcp.docs_v1.OptionalColor The background color of the text. If set, the color is either an RGB color or transparent, depending on the `color` field.
---@field strikethrough? boolean Whether or not the text is struck through.
---@field foregroundColor? gcp.docs_v1.OptionalColor The foreground color of the text. If set, the color is either an RGB color or transparent, depending on the `color` field.
---@field italic? boolean Whether or not the text is italicized.
---@field bold? boolean Whether or not the text is rendered as bold.
---@field smallCaps? boolean Whether or not the text is in small capital letters.
---@field fontSize? gcp.docs_v1.Dimension The size of the text's font.
---@field underline? boolean Whether or not the text is underlined.
---@field link? gcp.docs_v1.Link The hyperlink destination of the text. If unset, there's no link. Links are not inherited from parent text. Changing the link in an update request causes some other changes to the text style of the range: * When setting a link, the text foreground color will be updated to the default link color and the text will be underlined. If these fields are modified in the same request, those values will be used instead of the link defaults. * Setting a link on a text range that overlaps with an existing link will also update the existing link to point to the new URL. * Links are not settable on newline characters. As a result, setting a link on a text range that crosses a paragraph boundary, such as `"ABC\n123"`, will separate the newline character(s) into their own text runs. The link will be applied separately to the runs before and after the newline. * Removing a link will update the text style of the range to match the style of the preceding text (or the default text styles if the preceding text is another link) unless different styles are being set in the same request.
---@field weightedFontFamily? gcp.docs_v1.WeightedFontFamily The font family and rendered weight of the text. If an update request specifies values for both `weighted_font_family` and `bold`, the `weighted_font_family` is applied first, then `bold`. If `weighted_font_family#weight` is not set, it defaults to `400`. If `weighted_font_family` is set, then `weighted_font_family#font_family` must also be set with a non-empty value. Otherwise, a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field baselineOffset? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyleBaselineOffsetEnum|string The text's vertical offset from its normal position. Text with `SUPERSCRIPT` or `SUBSCRIPT` baseline offsets is automatically rendered in a smaller font size, computed based on the `font_size` field. Changes in this field don't affect the `font_size`.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.TextStyleBaselineOffsetEnum "BASELINE_OFFSET_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"SUPERSCRIPT"|"SUBSCRIPT"

---A mask that indicates which of the fields on the base TextStyle have been changed in this suggestion. For any field set to true, there's a new suggested value.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.TextStyleSuggestionState
---@field foregroundColorSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to foreground_color.
---@field italicSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to italic.
---@field baselineOffsetSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to baseline_offset.
---@field backgroundColorSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to background_color.
---@field underlineSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to underline.
---@field smallCapsSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to small_caps.
---@field boldSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to bold.
---@field fontSizeSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to font_size.
---@field weightedFontFamilySuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to weighted_font_family.
---@field linkSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to link.
---@field strikethroughSuggested? boolean Indicates if there was a suggested change to strikethrough.

---Unmerges cells in a Table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UnmergeTableCellsRequest
---@field tableRange? gcp.docs_v1.TableRange The table range specifying which cells of the table to unmerge. All merged cells in this range will be unmerged, and cells that are already unmerged will not be affected. If the range has no merged cells, the request will do nothing. If there is text in any of the merged cells, the text will remain in the "head" cell of the resulting block of unmerged cells. The "head" cell is the upper-left cell when the content direction is from left to right, and the upper-right otherwise.

---Updates a Post in a CommentThread or SuggestionThread. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The post is the headPost of a SuggestionThread. - The requesting user is not the author of the post.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateCommentPostRequest
---@field suggestionId? string The ID of the SuggestionThread which the post belongs to.
---@field content? string The new text of the comment, as plain text. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Docs editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. This field cannot be empty, and must not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field commentId? string The ID of the CommentThread which the post belongs to.
---@field postId? string The ID of the post being updated.

---Updates the DocumentStyle.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateDocumentStyleRequest
---@field documentStyle? gcp.docs_v1.DocumentStyle The styles to set on the document. Certain document style changes may cause other changes in order to mirror the behavior of the Docs editor. See the documentation of DocumentStyle for more information.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `document_style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the background, set `fields` to `"background"`.
---@field tabId? string The tab that contains the style to update. When omitted, the request applies to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If not provided, the request applies to the first tab in the document.

---Update the properties of a document tab.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateDocumentTabPropertiesRequest
---@field tabProperties? gcp.docs_v1.TabProperties The tab properties to update.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tab_properties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field.

---Updates the properties of a DropdownDefinition.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateDropdownDefinitionPropertiesRequest
---@field selectedOptionIdReplacements? gcp.docs_v1.StringMap A map of option IDs to their replacements, used to automatically reassign orphaned Dropdown chips when an option is deleted. The keys are the IDs of the options being deleted, and the values are the IDs of their replacement options. If an option being deleted is selected in one or more Dropdown chips in the document, a replacement entry for that option must be provided in this map, and the replacement option ID must exist in the updated DropdownDefinition. If a replacement is required but not provided, a 400 bad request error is returned. Options being deleted that are not selected in any Dropdown chips do not require a replacement. For example, if option A is being replaced by option B, the map should be `{"A": "B"}`.
---@field tabId? string The ID of the tab that contains the dropdown definition to update. When omitted, the request is applied to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.
---@field dropdownDefinitionId? string The ID of the DropdownDefinition to update.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `dropdown_definition_properties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. When `dropdown_definition_properties.options` is included in the field mask, the full, complete list of desired options must be provided in `dropdown_definition_properties.options`.
---@field dropdownDefinitionProperties? gcp.docs_v1.DropdownDefinitionProperties The properties to update.

---Updates the properties of a Dropdown.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateDropdownPropertiesRequest
---@field dropdownId? string Required. The Dropdown ID.
---@field tabId? string The ID of the tab that contains the dropdown to update. When omitted, the request is applied to the first tab. In a document containing a single tab: - If provided, must match the singular tab's ID. - If omitted, the request applies to the singular tab. In a document containing multiple tabs: - If provided, the request applies to the specified tab. - If omitted, the request applies to the first tab in the document.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `dropdown_properties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field.
---@field dropdownProperties? gcp.docs_v1.DropdownProperties The properties to update.

---Updates a named style.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateNamedStyleRequest
---@field fields? string The NamedStyle fields that should be updated. At least `named_style_type` must be specified. The root `named_style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example, to update the text style to bold, set `fields` to include `"text_style"` and `"text_style.bold"`. To update the paragraph style's alignment property, set `fields` to include `"paragraph_style"` and `"paragraph_style.alignment"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset. Specifying `"text_style"` or `"paragraph_style"` with an empty TextStyle or ParagraphStyle will reset all of its nested fields.
---@field namedStyle? gcp.docs_v1.NamedStyle The document style to update.
---@field tabId? string The document tab to update. By default, the update is applied to the first tab.

---Update the styling of all paragraphs that overlap with the given range.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateParagraphStyleRequest
---@field paragraphStyle? gcp.docs_v1.ParagraphStyle The styles to set on the paragraphs. Certain paragraph style changes may cause other changes in order to mirror the behavior of the Docs editor. See the documentation of ParagraphStyle for more information.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `paragraph_style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example, to update the paragraph style's alignment property, set `fields` to `"alignment"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field range? gcp.docs_v1.Range The range overlapping the paragraphs to style.

---Updates the SectionStyle.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateSectionStyleRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `section_style` is implied and must not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the left margin, set `fields` to `"margin_left"`.
---@field range? gcp.docs_v1.Range The range overlapping the sections to style. Because section breaks can only be inserted inside the body, the segment ID field must be empty.
---@field sectionStyle? gcp.docs_v1.SectionStyle The styles to be set on the section. Certain section style changes may cause other changes in order to mirror the behavior of the Docs editor. See the documentation of SectionStyle for more information.

---Updates the style of a range of table cells.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateTableCellStyleRequest
---@field tableCellStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableCellStyle The style to set on the table cells. When updating borders, if a cell shares a border with an adjacent cell, the corresponding border property of the adjacent cell is updated as well. Borders that are merged and invisible are not updated. Since updating a border shared by adjacent cells in the same request can cause conflicting border updates, border updates are applied in the following order: - `border_right` - `border_left` - `border_bottom` - `border_top`
---@field tableStartLocation? gcp.docs_v1.Location The location where the table starts in the document. When specified, the updates are applied to all the cells in the table.
---@field tableRange? gcp.docs_v1.TableRange The table range representing the subset of the table to which the updates are applied.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableCellStyle` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the table cell background color, set `fields` to `"backgroundColor"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.

---Updates the TableColumnProperties of columns in a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateTableColumnPropertiesRequest
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableColumnProperties` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the column width, set `fields` to `"width"`.
---@field tableStartLocation? gcp.docs_v1.Location The location where the table starts in the document.
---@field tableColumnProperties? gcp.docs_v1.TableColumnProperties The table column properties to update. If the value of `table_column_properties#width` is less than 5 points (5/72 inch), a 400 bad request error is returned.
---@field columnIndices? gcp.docs_v1.IntegerList The list of zero-based column indices whose property should be updated. If no indices are specified, all columns will be updated.

---Updates the TableRowStyle of rows in a table.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateTableRowStyleRequest
---@field tableRowStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TableRowStyle The styles to be set on the rows.
---@field rowIndices? gcp.docs_v1.IntegerList The list of zero-based row indices whose style should be updated. If no indices are specified, all rows will be updated.
---@field tableStartLocation? gcp.docs_v1.Location The location where the table starts in the document.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `tableRowStyle` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example to update the minimum row height, set `fields` to `"min_row_height"`.

---Update the styling of text.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.UpdateTextStyleRequest
---@field range? gcp.docs_v1.Range The range of text to style. The range may be extended to include adjacent newlines. If the range fully contains a paragraph belonging to a list, the paragraph's bullet is also updated with the matching text style. Ranges cannot be inserted inside a relative UpdateTextStyleRequest.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `text_style` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field. For example, to update the text style to bold, set `fields` to `"bold"`. To reset a property to its default value, include its field name in the field mask but leave the field itself unset.
---@field textStyle? gcp.docs_v1.TextStyle The styles to set on the text. If the value for a particular style matches that of the parent, that style will be set to inherit. Certain text style changes may cause other changes in order to to mirror the behavior of the Docs editor. See the documentation of TextStyle for more information.

---Represents a font family and weight of text.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.WeightedFontFamily
---@field weight? number The weight of the font. This field can have any value that's a multiple of `100` between `100` and `900`, inclusive. This range corresponds to the numerical values described in the CSS 2.1 Specification, [section 15.6](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/fonts.html#font-boldness), with non-numerical values disallowed. The default value is `400` ("normal"). The font weight makes up just one component of the rendered font weight. A combination of the `weight` and the text style's resolved `bold` value determine the rendered weight, after accounting for inheritance: * If the text is bold and the weight is less than `400`, the rendered weight is 400. * If the text is bold and the weight is greater than or equal to `400` but is less than `700`, the rendered weight is `700`. * If the weight is greater than or equal to `700`, the rendered weight is equal to the weight. * If the text is not bold, the rendered weight is equal to the weight.
---@field fontFamily? string The font family of the text. The font family can be any font from the Font menu in Docs or from [Google Fonts] (https://fonts.google.com/). If the font name is unrecognized, the text is rendered in `Arial`.

---Provides control over how write requests are executed.
---@class gcp.docs_v1.WriteControl
---@field targetRevisionId? string The optional target revision ID of the document the write request is applied to. If collaborator changes have occurred after the document was read using the API, the changes produced by this write request are applied against the collaborator changes. This results in a new revision of the document that incorporates both the collaborator changes and the changes in the request, with the Docs server resolving conflicting changes. When using target revision ID, the API client can be thought of as another collaborator of the document. The target revision ID can only be used to write to recent versions of a document. If the target revision is too far behind the latest revision, the request is not processed and returns a 400 bad request error. The request should be tried again after retrieving the latest version of the document. Usually a revision ID remains valid for use as a target revision for several minutes after it's read, but for frequently edited documents this window might be shorter.
---@field requiredRevisionId? string The optional revision ID of the document the write request is applied to. If this is not the latest revision of the document, the request is not processed and returns a 400 bad request error. When a required revision ID is returned in a response, it indicates the revision ID of the document after the request was applied.
---@field writeMode? gcp.docs_v1.WriteControlWriteModeEnum|string How the request updates should be applied to the document. If unspecified, the request updates will be applied as normal edits.

---@alias gcp.docs_v1.WriteControlWriteModeEnum "WRITE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EDIT"|"SUGGEST"

